  "design": {
    "identity": "Preserve reference exactly: massive coiled slate-blue ridged reef shell with pale barnacle holes, long ivory bony neck and hooked face, single cyan eye, hanging green algae, two long ivory scythe foreclaws and short supporting shell legs.",
    "idle": "Shell remains planted while long neck lifts and curls, foreclaw joints open and fold, algae swings with breathing in a clear seamless cycle.",
    "attack": "Retract head, raise both scythe foreclaws high, slash them LEFT in alternating heavy arcs, neck follows then recoil.",
    "cast": "Neck extends very high, shell mantle hinges open slightly, claws spread wide and cyan soul siphon gathers at mouth; close and lower.",
    "death": "Cyan eye extinguishes, scythe limbs fold inward, long neck slumps over grounded shell, algae and foreclaws settle coherently."
  }
